meta {
  name: Upload Catalog CSV
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/products/upload-csv
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(/path/to/catalog.csv)
}

docs {
  ## POST /api/products/upload-csv

  **Retailer only.** Bulk-imports products and variants from a CSV file.
  Also ingests body-fit measurements (`chest_cm`, `waist_cm`, `hip_cm`,
  `length_cm`, `inseam_cm`) for pgvector embedding generation when present.

  ### Authentication
  Requires a logged-in retailer **session cookie** (dashboard auth).

  ### CSV Column Reference
  | Column       | Required | Description                            |
  |--------------|----------|----------------------------------------|
  | product_id   | ✅       | Stable retailer-side SKU/code          |
  | product_name | ✅       | Display name                           |
  | category     | ✅       | Category slug (`shirt`, `pants`, etc.) |
  | gender       | ✅       | `male`, `female`, or `unisex`          |
  | brand        | ✅       | Brand name                             |
  | fabric       | ❌       | Fabric description                     |
  | price_egp    | ✅       | Price in Egyptian Pounds               |
  | image_url    | ✅       | HTTPS URL to the product image         |
  | size_label   | ✅       | Size label (S, M, L, XL, etc.)         |
  | chest_cm     | ❌       | Chest measurement for this size        |
  | waist_cm     | ❌       | Waist measurement for this size        |
  | hip_cm       | ❌       | Hip measurement for this size          |
  | length_cm    | ❌       | Length measurement for this size       |
  | inseam_cm    | ❌       | Inseam measurement for this size       |

  ### Success (200)
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "count": 25,
    "measurementErrors": [],
    "noMeasurementData": ["PROD-007"]
  }
  ```

  > **Note:** Products are **upserted** via `retailerId_productCode` composite key.
  > A `201` count means 25 product groups were processed; individual variants are
  > upserted independently. `measurementErrors` are non-blocking — the catalog write
  > succeeds even if measurement validation fails for a size row.
}
